/// The PDK's own view of the family runtime capabilities.
///
/// This package exists for one reason: a guest world's *imports* have to be
/// generated by a `wit_bindgen::generate!` that the PDK itself owns, or the
/// PDK cannot call them. `component.rs` already generates the whole
/// `indexer-plugin` world, and that one cannot be reused here — it generates
/// the indexer world's `export!`/`Guest` machinery along with its imports, and
/// its capability interface is `scryer:indexer/host@1.1.0`, an interface no
/// family component's host serves. A family artifact that named it would
/// carry a live import nothing satisfies and would fail to instantiate.
///
/// So this world imports the family-neutral capability interface and nothing
/// else: no exports, no second world, no host interface a family component
/// does not already have. wit-bindgen emits only the import bindings, and the
/// component-type metadata merged into the final artifact adds exactly this
/// one import — tree-shaken away again in a guest (an indexer, say) whose
/// reachable code never names it.
package scryer:pdk@1.0.0;

/// Import-only: the typed async capability surface, for the PDK to call.
world runtime-imports {
  import scryer:runtime/host@1.0.0;
}
